---
title: Pumpkin pie
servings: 8
yield: one 9-inch deep-dish pie
tags: [american, vegetarian, thanksgiving, holiday, fall, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
source: Adapted from The Great Pumpkin Pie in tdstein/recipes (MIT), https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tdstein/recipes/main/recipes/The%20Great%20Pumpkin%20Pie.cook
---

> Use one disc of the crust from Buttery pie crust (baking/pies-and-tarts).

== Sugared cranberries ==

Put the @cranberries{1%cup} in a #large bowl{}. Bring @granulated sugar{1%cup} and @water{} to a simmer in a #medium saucepan{}, stirring until the sugar dissolves.

Cool the syrup ~{5%minutes}, pour it over the berries and leave them ~{6%hours} or overnight.

Drain them, toss in another @granulated sugar{1%cup} and spread them on a #baking sheet{} lined with parchment. Leave to dry at least ~{2%hours}.

== Crust ==

Heat the oven to 375°F (190°C).

Roll the dough to a 12-inch round on a lightly floured counter and fit it into a #9-inch deep-dish pie plate{}. Crimp the edge.

Beat the @egg{1} with @milk{1%tbsp} and brush it over the rim. Line the shell, fill with #pie weights{} and bake ~{10%minutes}. Lift out the weights.

== Filling ==

Whisk the @pumpkin purée{15%oz}, @eggs{3} and @light brown sugar{1.25%cups} in a large bowl.

Whisk in the @cornstarch{1%tbsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp}, @cinnamon{1.5%tsp}, @ginger{1/2%tsp}, @nutmeg{1/4%tsp}, @cloves{1/8%tsp} and @black pepper{1/8%tsp}. Then whisk in the @heavy cream{1%cup} and @milk{1/4%cup}.

Fill the crust about three quarters full. Bake ~{25%minutes}, cover the edge with foil, then bake ~{30%minutes} to 35 minutes more, until the centre is nearly set.

Cool on a #wire rack{} at least ~{3%hours}. Top with the sugared cranberries.

> Keep the pie in the fridge up to 5 days, the cranberries up to 3.
